<title>UK: LIFFE sugar mixed in PM trade, directionless.</title>
<headline>LIFFE sugar mixed in PM trade, directionless.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIFFE sugar was tightly mixed in afternoon trade, with nearby months firmer, while more distant contracts were lower.</p>
<p>By 1500 GMT October was 20 cents higher at $321.20 inj a volume of 582 out of a total 1,686 lots, making it the most active month.</p>
<p>Traders saw no great direction in the market. One described it as &quot;drifting.&quot; &quot;20 cents up (on October) isn't anything to get excited about,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
